-- router.talk: a computed message name in `send` (ADR 0057). Part of the
-- messages-and-waiting case. The name is lowered first, below the
-- arguments, and the named sends carry only the argument count.

on route next, order, board
  send (next) with order to board
  send (next) with order to board and wait
  wait for all
    send ("move:" & "to:") with order, "e4" to board and wait
  end wait
  return it
end route
